{"kind":"stack","id":"water-cycle-s1","title":"The water cycle: evaporation and condensation","theme":{"background":"#e8f4fb","foreground":"#1a3a4a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Evaporation"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Evaporation is when liquid water heats up and turns into water vapour, a gas that rises into the air."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Condensation"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Condensation is when water vapour cools down and turns back into tiny liquid droplets, forming clouds."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c3-p","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What does the sun mainly do in the water cycle?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Heats water so it evaporates","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Makes rain fall from clouds","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Turns rivers into salt water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which process turns water vapour back into liquid droplets to form clouds?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Evaporation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Condensation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Freezing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Where does water evaporate fastest?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"In a cold fridge","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"On a sunny, warm day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"In a dark, cold cellar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c6-p","picto":"river"},{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Liam leaves a bowl of water on the windowsill on a hot day. Later, the bowl is nearly empty. What should he think?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"The water evaporated into the air","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"The water soaked into the table","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Well done, Liam! The heat from the sun gave the water enough energy to become vapour. The vapour rose and mixed with the air."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Not quite. Water does not soak into a table. The water turned into vapour and floated away into the air."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which is bigger, the rate of evaporation in summer or in winter?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Winter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"end"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Summer","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"end"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"end","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"end-h","content":"You finished the water cycle quiz!"},{"type":"text","id":"end-m","content":"Great work exploring evaporation and condensation. Keep watching the water around you."}],"actions":[]}}
